     :say "A multi-row atomic write unit: fn-row + N slot-rows + N fn-slot junctions, appending each success to a shared `journal` atom. Shows how one logical create fans out into many graph rows.")
    (:key "crud/apply-create-rollback" :n 7 :gi 86 :defn "apply-create-rollback" :ns "graphden.crud.entities.record-type" :file "src/graphden/crud/entities/record_type.clj" :line 114 :lang "clj" :mins 1.8 :head "(defn apply-create-rollback" :see nil :refs nil :siblings (("crud/apply-create-record-type-body" . "apply-create-record-type-body"))
     :say "The `:try` on-throw partner: replay the `journal` in reverse, best-effort deleting each row. This is how atomicity is achieved here WITHOUT a DB transaction — the compensating half of the body above.")
    (:key "crud/apply-create-core" :n 8 :gi 87 :defn "apply-create-core" :ns "graphden.crud.entities" :file "src/graphden/crud/entities.clj" :line 555 :lang "clj" :mins 4.6 :head "(defn apply-create-core" :see nil :refs (("web/write-rej" . "write-rej")) :siblings (("crud/create-entity" . "create-entity"))
     :say "The atomic core for generic creates: create-or-humanise-error, a post-create whole-fn type-check, and the rename-slot side-effect. Since error-tolerance Phase 2 an ORDINARY type-check failure no longer rolls the row back — the write is kept and the diagnostics surface as `:type-warnings` on the success envelope. One class is carved out: a SECRET-flow diagnostic still deletes the row and returns the legacy `{:error …}` (the guarantee must not rest on the derived diagnostics store — docs/SECRETS.md).")
    (:key "crud/type-check-fn-after-mutation!" :n 9 :gi 88 :defn "type-check-fn-after-mutation!" :ns "graphden.crud.type-check" :file "src/graphden/crud/type_check.clj" :line 371 :lang "clj" :mins 4.9 :head "(defn type-check-fn-after-mutation!" :see (("types/check-fn-def!" . "check-fn-def!")) :refs nil :siblings nil
     :say "Reconstructs the touched fn-def and runs `check-fn-def!` after a mutation, recording failures in (and clearing fixes from) the per-branch diagnostics store. This is the type-check-on-write that `apply-create-core` relies on — an ill-typed fn persists, but never silently: every save re-derives its diagnostics. The `:reject-secret?` option is the security carve-out: a secret-involving failure is flagged `:secret? true` and NOT recorded — the caller rolls the write back and hard-rejects.")
    (:key "crud/notify-after-write!" :n 10 :gi 89 :defn "notify-after-write!" :ns "graphden.crud.entities.invalidation" :file "src/graphden/crud/entities/invalidation.clj" :line 221 :lang "clj" :mins 4.8 :head "(defn notify-after-write!" :see nil :refs (("storage/make-emitter" . "make-emitter")) :siblings nil
     :say "The post-persist step: invalidate caches and broadcast a NOTIFY delta so sibling pods rebuild the affected fns. How a committed write becomes visible fleet-wide.")
    (:key "crud/resolve-fn" :n 11 :gi 90 :defn "resolve-fn" :ns "graphden.crud.fn-execution.lookup" :file "src/graphden/crud/fn_execution/lookup.clj" :line 84 :lang "clj" :mins 1.2 :head "(defn resolve-fn" :see nil :refs nil :siblings nil
     :say "Translates the `/api/execute` `{:fn-id | :fn-name}` request into the full `:fn` row in one round-trip — the lookup that begins the execution + persist path.")
    (:key "crud/public-free-entries" :n 12 :gi 91 :defn "public-free-entries" :ns "graphden.executor.compile.surface" :file "src/graphden/executor/compile/surface.clj" :line 85 :lang "clj" :mins 5.7 :head "(defn public-free-entries" :see nil :refs (("executor/build-ref-renames" . "build-ref-renames")) :siblings nil
     :say "The one free-arg surface every name-facing consumer reads — the Run form's arg list, the service create-guard, the canvas's deep-free placeholders: the name walker's public names plus the HOF closure captures the entry walker finds by descending into HOF targets, minus everything an enclosing scope supplies (lambda params by alpha-equivalence, env-bindings), one hole per slot identity. Read it before touching any of the three: they agree by construction.")
    (:key "crud/apply-execute" :n 13 :gi 92 :defn "apply-execute" :ns "graphden.crud.fn-execution" :file "src/graphden/crud/fn_execution.clj" :line 120 :lang "clj" :mins 2.1 :head "(defn apply-execute" :see nil :refs nil :siblings nil
     :say "The `/api/execute` orchestrator: resolve fn + version + free-arg slots, acquire a concurrency slot, submit the future, and dispatch on succeeded / pending / failed. The spine of the execute write path — and where it hands off to the executor from the first block.")
    (:key "crud/create-pending-with-args!" :n 14 :gi 93 :defn "create-pending-with-args!" :ns "graphden.crud.fn-execution.persist" :file "src/graphden/crud/fn_execution/persist.clj" :line 340 :lang "clj" :mins 1.5 :head "(defn create-pending-with-args!" :see nil :refs nil :siblings (("crud/write-finished!" . "write-finished!"))
     :say "Atomically writes the `:fn-execution` row plus its per-arg (`:fn-execution-arg` / `-item`) rows — the concrete `an execution becomes persisted graph rows` step.")
