     :say "Updates the execution row with the future's terminal outcome (result / error / cancelled, with taint redaction). Closes the loop so a polled execution reflects final persisted state.")
    (:key "crud/render-repr" :n 16 :gi 95 :defn "render-repr" :ns "graphden.crud.value-repr" :file "src/graphden/crud/value_repr.clj" :line 77 :lang "clj" :mins 2.5 :head "(defn render-repr" :see nil :refs (("editor/enterArgValueEditMode" . "enterArgValueEditMode") ("platform/sanitize-hiccup" . "sanitize-hiccup")) :siblings nil
     :say "Typed value representations (docs/EXECUTION.md § Typed value representations) — the execute-result pane's first dispatch tier and the value-form registry's read-side sibling: resolve a repr fn through the graph-held `:_value-repr-registry` (declared/inferred return type first, literal classification as fallback), execute it as a pure `value → hiccup` fn under the `:allowed-effects #{}` runtime gate, then push the output through the `web.hiccup-sanitize` allowlist before the editor inlines it into its own DOM.")
    (:key "crud/resolve-form" :n 17 :gi 96 :defn "resolve-form" :ns "graphden.crud.value-form" :file "src/graphden/crud/value_form.clj" :line 399 :lang "clj" :mins 3.3 :head "(defn resolve-form" :see nil :refs nil :siblings (("crud/build-form" . "build-form"))
     :say "The other direction of `render-repr`: EDITING a value. A slot's effective type is classified into a form-descriptor tree — record, list, union, or leaf — purely, with aliases resolved and variants desugared, so the editor never has to know the type algebra. A depth guard keeps a recursive record type from unfolding forever.")
    (:key "crud/build-form" :n 18 :gi 97 :defn "build-form" :ns "graphden.crud.value-form" :file "src/graphden/crud/value_form.clj" :line 720 :lang "clj" :mins 6.0 :head "(defn build-form" :see nil :refs nil :siblings (("crud/resolve-form" . "resolve-form"))
     :say "…and the descriptor becomes hiccup: a record is a labelled fieldset, a union a branch `<select>` plus one sub-form per branch (the backend pre-selects the branch the current value fits), a leaf goes through the form-fn registry the `app/forms` package populates. This is what `GET /partials/value-form` returns and what the Inspector swaps in — server-rendered, HTMX-wired (docs/PARTIALS.md).")
    (:key "crud/run-captured!" :n 19 :gi 98 :defn "run-captured!" :ns "graphden.crud.debug-capture" :file "src/graphden/crud/debug_capture.clj" :line 285 :lang "clj" :mins 2.3 :head "(defn run-captured!" :see nil :refs nil :siblings nil
     :say "The «catch next request» debugger entry (docs/EXECUTION.md § Debug): a one-shot, TTL-bounded, org+branch-keyed trap consumed in `branch-router/ring-callable-for-ctx` runs the next matching HTTP request through this wrapper — Debug path-trace bound, sanitized request + response persisted as a standard `:fn-execution` row — so a live handler run replays through the same call-tree UI as a traced `/api/execute`.")
    (:key "crud/create-secret" :n 20 :gi 99 :defn "create-secret" :ns "graphden.crud.secrets" :file "src/graphden/crud/secrets.clj" :line 348 :lang "clj" :mins 3.0 :head "(defn create-secret" :see (("types/taint-with-secret-if-tainted" . "taint-with-secret-if-tainted")) :refs nil :siblings nil
     :say "The write path that must not leak (docs/SECRETS.md): one `POST /api/secrets` atomically creates the OpenBao value, its custom-metadata, and the graphden fn-row + path-binding — with a vault-delete rollback if the graph half fails. The secret VALUE never enters the graph; only the path does, on a `:secret-leaf` child the executor auto-derefs through the ctx's vault handle. Note the shape: this public defn is thin orchestration over the same per-stage helpers the `:cond` in `app/secrets/fns.edn` consumes, so the Clojure and the graph path can never diverge.")
    (:key "crud/run-tests!" :n 21 :gi 100 :defn "run-tests!" :ns "graphden.crud.test-runs" :file "src/graphden/crud/test_runs.clj" :line 193 :lang "clj" :mins 4.2 :head "(defn run-tests!" :see nil :refs nil :siblings nil
     :say "The tests subsystem (docs/TESTS.md) rides everything above: a test is a fn in a `tests`-segment namespace, executed through `apply-execute` with `{}` args (pass = no throw), its status the newest execution of its CURRENT version — so an edited test reads `stale` by construction, no bookkeeping. After EACH test it nudges the `test:updated` NOTIFY, which is what moves the Explorer's dots one by one under the ✓ tests lens (its SSE ping stream). Note the `platform?` arm: the SHIPPED packages carry their own `*.tests` modules (`core.tests`, `web.tests`, …), and a default all-tests run skips them — the rule is OWNERSHIP (`packages.owned/owned-fn-id?`, package-synced this boot), not intent, so a tenant's Run all spends its budget on its own tests. The platform set is gated by its own Clojure anchor instead.")
    (:key "crud/schedule-affected!" :n 22 :gi 101 :defn "schedule-affected!" :ns "graphden.crud.test-autorun" :file "src/graphden/crud/test_autorun.clj" :line 170 :lang "clj" :mins 2.4 :head "(defn schedule-affected!" :see nil :refs nil :siblings nil
     :say "Auto-run on writes: from `invalidate!`'s seeds, walk the compile-deps REVERSE closure (the service-restart blast walk), intersect with the branch's tests, gate on an EMPTY effect closure, and re-run debounced on a conveyed-bindings future with `:allowed-effects #{}` as the runtime backstop.")
    (:key "crud/list-all-graph-entities" :n 23 :gi 102 :defn "list-all-graph-entities" :ns "graphden.crud.entities.list" :file "src/graphden/crud/entities/list.clj" :line 624 :lang "clj" :mins 3.6 :head "(defn list-all-graph-entities" :see nil :refs nil :siblings nil
     :say "The read side the editor lives on. One call, one shared lazy `graph-list-env` over the graph-cache, and a `scope` that picks a projection: the sidebar tree (namespaces + counts, O(namespaces)), one namespace's leaves, a search, a subtree, or the full dump. Every fn row is tagged with a `:role` so Types vs Functions is decided server-side. When the editor feels slow after a write, this is where to look — it is what every refresh re-reads.")))
  (:id "packages" :title "Packages — the graph's content" :status "toured" :mins 104.9 :summary "How fns.edn + impls.clj become base-fns and fn-defs; the loader,
             load order, and the first-party package tree — then the inverse:
             export, the ref wire form, and the publish/install registry."
